423 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 260 0 R
/T (The proposed system is a real-time Sign Language Recognition System designed to interpret hand gestures and convert them into meaningful text output. The system captures live video input using a webcam and processes it using computer vision techniques to detect and analyze hand movements. The system uses MediaPipe for accurate hand landmark detection and a machine learning model such as Feedforward Neural Network \(FNN\) or LSTM for gesture classification. )
/E (The proposed system is a real-time Sign Language Recognition System designed to interpret hand gestures and convert them into meaningful text output. The system captures live video input using a webcam and processes it using computer vision techniques to detect and analyze hand movements. The system uses MediaPipe for accurate hand landmark detection and a machine learning model such as Feedforward Neural Network \(FNN\) or LSTM for gesture classification. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
424 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 260 0 R
/T (     It focuses on recognizing predefined static gestures efficiently and  displaying the corresponding output in real time. The main objective of this system is to reduce the communication gap between individuals who use sign language and those who do not understand it. The system is designed to be simple, fast, and user-friendly, making it suitable for real-time applications and future enhancements.)
/E (     It focuses on recognizing predefined static gestures efficiently and  displaying the corresponding output in real time. The main objective of this system is to reduce the communication gap between individuals who use sign language and those who do not understand it. The system is designed to be simple, fast, and user-friendly, making it suitable for real-time applications and future enhancements.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
