511 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 266 0 R
/T (Sign language recognition has gained significant attention in recent years with the advancement of machine learning and computer vision technologies. Many earlier systems used image processing techniques and Convolutional Neural Networks \(CNN\) to classify hand gestures from static images. Some systems used sensor-based gloves to capture hand movements, which offered high precision but were expensive and not practical for everyday use. Recent studies have focused on vision-based approaches using cameras and frameworks like MediaPipe for efficient hand tracking and landmark detection. Compared to previous methods, this project uses a real-time webcam-based system with MediaPipe and a neural network model \(FNN/LSTM\), making it more efficient, cost-effective, and suitable for real-time applications.)
/E (Sign language recognition has gained significant attention in recent years with the advancement of machine learning and computer vision technologies. Many earlier systems used image processing techniques and Convolutional Neural Networks \(CNN\) to classify hand gestures from static images. Some systems used sensor-based gloves to capture hand movements, which offered high precision but were expensive and not practical for everyday use. Recent studies have focused on vision-based approaches using cameras and frameworks like MediaPipe for efficient hand tracking and landmark detection. Compared to previous methods, this project uses a real-time webcam-based system with MediaPipe and a neural network model \(FNN/LSTM\), making it more efficient, cost-effective, and suitable for real-time applications.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
