516 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 267 0 R
/T (Earlier systems mainly used image processing techniques and Convolutional Neural Networks \(CNN\) to recognize hand gestures from static images. These methods focused on extracting features such as hand shape, edges, and contours from images. While these systems achieved good accuracy, they required large datasets and high computational power. Additionally, most of these models were limited to offline processing and were not suitable for real-time applications.)
/E (Earlier systems mainly used image processing techniques and Convolutional Neural Networks \(CNN\) to recognize hand gestures from static images. These methods focused on extracting features such as hand shape, edges, and contours from images. While these systems achieved good accuracy, they required large datasets and high computational power. Additionally, most of these models were limited to offline processing and were not suitable for real-time applications.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
517 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 267 0 R
/T (Some research introduced glove-based systems equipped with sensors to capture hand movements, finger positions, and orientation. These systems provided high accuracy and precise gesture detection. However, they were expensive, required additional hardware, and were not convenient for daily use. Due to these limitations, sensor- based systems are less preferred in practical applications.)
/E (Some research introduced glove-based systems equipped with sensors to capture hand movements, finger positions, and orientation. These systems provided high accuracy and precise gesture detection. However, they were expensive, required additional hardware, and were not convenient for daily use. Due to these limitations, sensor- based systems are less preferred in practical applications.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
518 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 267 0 R
/T (Recent advancements focus on vision-based systems that use cameras and computer vision techniques for gesture recognition. Frameworks like MediaPipe enable efficient hand tracking and extraction of hand landmarks in real time.In this project, a vision- based approach is used along with a machine learning model \(FNN/LSTM\) to achieve accurate and fast gesture recognition.)
/E (Recent advancements focus on vision-based systems that use cameras and computer vision techniques for gesture recognition. Frameworks like MediaPipe enable efficient hand tracking and extraction of hand landmarks in real time.In this project, a vision- based approach is used along with a machine learning model \(FNN/LSTM\) to achieve accurate and fast gesture recognition.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
