669 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 284 0 R
/T (Implementation is an important phase in the development of the Sign Language Recognition System, where the designed system is converted into a working application. The system is implemented using Python programming language along with libraries such as OpenCV, MediaPipe, and TensorFlow. The implementation begins with capturing real-time video input using a webcam. OpenCV is used to process the video frames, while MediaPipe is used to detect the hand and extract 21 landmark points. These landmarks are then preprocessed and converted into feature vectors. A machine learning model such as Feedforward Neural Network \(FNN\) or Long Short-Term Memory \(LSTM\) is trained using the collected dataset. The trained model is then integrated into the system for real-time gesture prediction. The system continuously captures frames, processes the input, and predicts the gesture using the trained model. The predicted output is displayed as text on the user interface. The implementation ensures that the system works efficiently in real time and provides accurate results under suitable conditions.)
/E (Implementation is an important phase in the development of the Sign Language Recognition System, where the designed system is converted into a working application. The system is implemented using Python programming language along with libraries such as OpenCV, MediaPipe, and TensorFlow. The implementation begins with capturing real-time video input using a webcam. OpenCV is used to process the video frames, while MediaPipe is used to detect the hand and extract 21 landmark points. These landmarks are then preprocessed and converted into feature vectors. A machine learning model such as Feedforward Neural Network \(FNN\) or Long Short-Term Memory \(LSTM\) is trained using the collected dataset. The trained model is then integrated into the system for real-time gesture prediction. The system continuously captures frames, processes the input, and predicts the gesture using the trained model. The predicted output is displayed as text on the user interface. The implementation ensures that the system works efficiently in real time and provides accurate results under suitable conditions.)
/Pg 41 0 R
