/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 295 0 R
/T (The Sign Language Recognition System successfully demonstrates the use of computer vision and machine learning techniques for real-time gesture recognition. The system is capable of accurately identifying predefined hand gestures using MediaPipe and a trained neural network model. The project follows a structured approach including data collection, preprocessing, model building, and real-time implementation. The system provides fast and efficient performance and is able to convert hand gestures into readable text, helping to reduce the communication gap for hearing and speech impaired individuals. Although the system performs well under controlled conditions, its accuracy may vary with changes in lighting and gesture variations. With further improvements such as larger datasets, advanced models, and additional features, the system can be enhanced for real-world applications and scalability.)
/E (The Sign Language Recognition System successfully demonstrates the use of computer vision and machine learning techniques for real-time gesture recognition. The system is capable of accurately identifying predefined hand gestures using MediaPipe and a trained neural network model. The project follows a structured approach including data collection, preprocessing, model building, and real-time implementation. The system provides fast and efficient performance and is able to convert hand gestures into readable text, helping to reduce the communication gap for hearing and speech impaired individuals. Although the system performs well under controlled conditions, its accuracy may vary with changes in lighting and gesture variations. With further improvements such as larger datasets, advanced models, and additional features, the system can be enhanced for real-world applications and scalability.)
/Pg 52 0 R
/K [6]
>>
