2007 0 obj
<<
/Title (Sign language recognition has gained significant attention in recent years with the advancement of machine learning and computer vision technologies. Many earlier systems used image processing techniques and Convolutional Neural Networks \(CNN\) to classify hand gestures from static images. Some systems used sensor-based gloves to capture hand movements, which offered high precision but were expensive and not practical for everyday use. Recent studies have focused on vision-based approaches using cameras and frameworks like MediaPipe for efficient hand tracking and landmark detection. Compared to previous methods, this project uses a real-time webcam-based system with MediaPipe and a neural network model \(FNN/LSTM\), making it more efficient, cost-effective, and suitable for real-time applications.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2003 0 R
/Next 2008 0 R
>>
endobj
2008 0 obj
<<
/Title (REAL TIME SYSTEM FOR SIGN LANGUAGE RECOGNITION)
/Dest [24 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2003 0 R
/Prev 2007 0 R
>>
endobj
2009 0 obj
<<
/Title (Some research introduced glove-based systems equipped with sensors to capture hand movements, finger positions, and orientation. These systems provided high accuracy and precise gesture detection. However, they were expensive, required additional hardware, and were not convenient for daily use. Due to these limitations, sensor- based systems are less preferred in practical applications.)
/Dest [24 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2005 0 R
>>
endobj
